  "behavior": [
    "Literal integer-array allocation strides 1..255, including 56-byte arrays, use the existing typed scaled-address action.",
    "Bounded shift/add decomposition accumulates the modulo-64-bit address in already-owned RCX/R8. Power-of-two instruction streams and physical clobber ownership are retained.",
    "Stack i32 descriptors still require scale four, rejected before mutation; read-only table actions retain their power-of-two and shape rules.",
    "All 255 scales execute against independent wrapping integer multiplication across 11475 cases per unit run. Native fixtures cover 56-byte, padded 12-byte, nested 15-byte, returned/reloaded 255-byte addresses and guarded 56-byte stores.",
    "Five permanent native functions pass direct/release routes in three modes with live values, clobbering helper calls, negative indexes, wrapping addresses and guards."
  ],
  "known_boundaries": [
    "Zero or greater-than-255 allocation strides; unknown/named/struct/floating array layouts; nondefault pointer address spaces/index widths; unsupported operand forms.",
    "Descriptor and read-only-table scale rules are unchanged. No new machine instruction or register-allocation policy.",
    "Fibonacci now reaches composed-block-load-ptr: an ordinary i32 load rejects its RAX pointer home during transaction seal. A retained loop reproduces it and Clang accepts the loop. Typed pointer staging, narrower call ABIs and whole-program execution remain later work."
  ],
